      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fort Madison was founded as the first permanent U.S. fort on the Mississippi in 1808.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Madison%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The fort was renamed Fort Madison in honor of President James Madison shortly after its original name, Fort Belle View.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://fortmadison-ia.com/280/History-of-Fort-Madison",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Sheaffer Pen Company, founded in 1907, built its factory on the former fort site, and its parking lot later yielded the fort’s blockhouse during excavations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        12,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Madison%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 1965 archaeological dig in the Sheaffer factory parking lot uncovered the fort’s central blockhouse and officers’ quarter foundations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Madison%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic fort site was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1973.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Madison%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Two railroads, BNSF and Union Pacific, still serve Fort Madison, echoing its early role as a transportation hub.",
